# Global authority (project hard rule)

This workspace **follows** the machine-global Cursor rules in `~/.cursor/rules/`.

Local copies under `.cursor/rules/` exist so the same pipeline is visible in-repo.
If local and global ever diverge, **global wins**.

## Canonical pipeline

1. Read `.cursor/SESSION_HANDOFF.md`
2. Capture asks in `.cursor/REQUIREMENTS.md` (`requirements-manager` / Tiny extract)
3. `adaptive-workflow` unless Tiny
4. Implement with global skills (`~/.cursor/skills/`, see `.cursor/GLOBAL_SKILL_SET.md`)
5. `acceptance-review` is the **only** Pass / Pass-with-follow-up / Fail authority

## Do not

- Invent a second planning / Pass / handoff system for this repo
- Run brainstorming HARD-GATE, llm-council-as-default, verification-loop-as-Pass, or other demoted gates as peer authorities (see `.cursor/SKILL_COMPATIBILITY_AND_COMBOS.md`)
- Shrink broad user scope silently
- Skip acceptance because the ask was informal

## Project-only notes (non-pipeline)

- Next.js guidance in `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` stays for framework APIs
- MPI UI taste skills under `.cursor/skills/` are domain helpers, not Pass authorities
